    {
      "id": "definition",
      "type": "definition",
      "heading": "Glossary term: Shadow",
      "body": "A shadow is an area where light from one object is blocked by another object. For example, during a total solar eclipse, the Moon blocks the Sun and casts a shadow on part of the Earth. A shadow always points away from a light source",
